---
layout: base.njk
title: "Adnan Ahmed Siddiqui | Cloud & EUC Architecture"
home: true
permalink: "/"
---
{%- set list = collections.articles -%}
<header class="band home-band"><div class="wrap band-in home-in">
  <div class="home-text">
    <p class="chip">Cloud architecture<span>Azure, AVD, Windows 365</span></p>
    <h1>Architecting Enterprise Azure &amp; End-User Computing</h1>
    <p class="band-deck">Production blueprints, Cloud Adoption Framework landing zones and hands-on architectures across Azure, AVD, Windows 365, Citrix and Intune. Every Azure fact is checked against Microsoft Learn.</p>
    <p class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href="/azure-landing-zone/">Read the Landing Zone series</a><a class="btn ghost-on" href="{{ site.repo }}">GitHub repositories</a></p>
  </div>
  <nav class="home-start" aria-label="Where to start">
    <p class="hs-h">Where to start</p>
    <a href="/start-here/"><strong>Start here</strong><span>How the site is organized and in which order to read</span></a>
    <a href="/azure-landing-zone/"><strong>Azure Landing Zone</strong><span>{{ collections.liveSeries[0].posts.length }} articles, from first idea to a working platform</span></a>
    <a href="/labs/"><strong>Labs and code</strong><span>Reference files that go with the articles</span></a>
  </nav>
</div></header>

<section class="sec" aria-labelledby="ser-h"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><h2 id="ser-h">Series</h2><a class="more" href="/articles/">All articles</a></div>
  <div class="series-grid">
    {%- for s in collections.liveSeries %}{% set tp = s | topicOf %}
    <a class="scard" href="/{{ s.slug }}/">
      <span class="skick">{{ tp.name }}</span>
      <strong>{{ s.title }}</strong>
      <span class="sbl">{{ s.blurb | clip(150) }}</span>
      <span class="smeta">{{ s.posts.length }} articles</span>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec alt" aria-labelledby="new-h"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><h2 id="new-h">Latest articles</h2><a class="more" href="/articles/">All articles</a></div>
  <ul class="alist">
    {%- for p in list | mixLatest(articleMeta, 6, 2) %}{% set ser = p.data.tags | seriesOf %}{% set meta = articleMeta[p.data.order] %}
    <li><a href="{{ p.url }}">
      <span class="ak">{{ ser.name }}{% if meta %} · <time datetime="{{ meta.published }}">{{ meta.published | longDate }}</time>{% endif %}</span>
      <strong>{{ p.data.title }}</strong>
      <span class="ad">{{ p.data.deck | clip(190) }}</span>
      <span class="am">{{ p.templateContent | readingTime }} min read</span>
    </a></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</div></section>

<section class="sec" aria-label="Labs and about"><div class="wrap duo">
  <div class="duo-card">
    <h2>Labs and code</h2>
    <p>Reference files and lab steps that go with the articles live in a public GitHub repo.</p>
    <p><a class="btn ghost" href="{{ site.repo }}">Open the Azure_landing_zone repo</a></p>
  </div>
  <div class="duo-card">
    <h2>About the author</h2>
    <p><strong>{{ site.author }}</strong>, {{ site.role }}. Each article is checked against Microsoft Learn before it goes out.</p>
    <p><a class="btn ghost" href="/about/">About the site and the author</a></p>
  </div>
</div></section>
